WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.316
Want to save PowerPoint as video?

2
00:00:03.366 --> 00:00:06.903
You have two sensible options, and they suit different jobs.

3
00:00:06.953 --> 00:00:09.297
Here's how to pick the right one for your deck.

4
00:00:09.797 --> 00:00:15.494
PowerPoint's own export plays your animations exactly as designed, with your real voice.

5
00:00:15.544 --> 00:00:16.817
The catch?

6
00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:20.615
Stumble on slide 12, and you re-record slide 12.

7
00:00:21.115 --> 00:00:27.497
A dedicated converter reads your speaker notes aloud, adds captions and times everything to the speech.

8
00:00:27.547 --> 00:00:30.843
The trade-off is a synthetic voice instead of your own.

9
00:00:31.343 --> 00:00:34.578
Take one headline about new starters' laptops.

10
00:00:34.628 --> 00:00:38.096
Record it yourself, and every change means a new take.

11
00:00:38.146 --> 00:00:41.349
Type it into the notes, and a change is one quick edit.

12
00:00:41.849 --> 00:00:43.389
Many people use both.

13
00:00:43.439 --> 00:00:51.378
A leader's quarterly message suits their own voice, while an onboarding module that changes every few months suits a converter.

14
00:00:52.249 --> 00:00:56.100
Ordinary slides in, extraordinary video out.

15
00:00:56.150 --> 00:01:01.499
On Pro, a.i. directs your video, tightening the story and timing each scene.

16
00:01:01.549 --> 00:01:04.995
Try Basic first at powerpoint2vid.com.

